  "finding_info": {
    "uid": "2011a6085a20fe4a6e8aa514ba1305b1",
    "title": "Dynamic-linker preload hijack",
    "desc": "A program set up a shared-library preload - an LD_PRELOAD / LD_AUDIT in a command's environment, or a write to /etc/ld.so.preload (or an ld.so.conf.d drop). The dynamic linker loads a preloaded object into every dynamically-linked process it starts, so an attacker uses it to inject code, hook libc calls, hide processes (libprocesshider) or escalate from a setuid binary (MITRE T1574.006). A system-wide /etc/ld.so.preload is a classic userland-rootkit foothold. Ordinary builds set LD_LIBRARY_PATH, not LD_PRELOAD, so this is deliberately narrow.",
    "analytic": {
      "type_id": 1,
      "type": "Rule",
      "name": "ld_preload_hijack",
